-- title:
--   Admissible rigidified family over the reduced edge chart
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, $k$ an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, and $\iota\colon \mathbb{Z}_{p^2}=W(\mathbb{F}_{p^2})\to W(k)$ a ring homomorphism; write $\bar j$ for $\iota$ followed by the quotient map $W(k)\to W(k)/pW(k)$ by the ideal generated by $p$. Let $\Phi$ be a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module over $W(k)/pW(k)$, i.e. a commutative formal group law in two variables with an action of $\mathbb{Z}_{p^2}$ and an endomorphism $\varpi$ satisfying $\varpi\circ\varpi=[p]$ and $\varpi\circ[a]=[\sigma a]\circ\varpi$, subject to: $\Phi$ is special for $\bar j$ (the weight spaces `lieZero` and `lieOne` of $\mathrm{Lie}\,\Phi$ are complementary and both invertible), $\Phi$ has height $4$ (the kernel of $[p]$ has degree $p^4$), `lieZero` is contained in the kernel of the linear part `lieVarpi` of $\varpi$ on $\mathrm{Lie}\,\Phi$, and the graded pieces of degree $0$ and $1$ of the Cartier module of $\Phi$ relative to $\bar j$ are complementary ($hc_\Phi$). Let $r_\Phi$ be an additive map from $\mathbb{Z}_p^2$ to the $N$-module of the graded Cartier module data attached to $(\Phi,\bar j,hc_\Phi)$ such that for every canonical $L$-map $L$ for that data, $r_\Phi$ carries all of $\mathbb{Z}_p^2$ bijectively onto the degree-$0$ $\eta$-piece `etaPiece L … 0`. Let $g\in\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_p)$ have matrix $\mathrm{diag}(p,1)$. Then there exists a rigidified triple $t$ over the edge-chart ring $E=$ `EdgeFamily.edgeRingCharP p (WittVector p k ⧸ pIdeal p (WittVector p k))` — by definition the localisation `chartERing` of the edge quotient ring over $W(k)/pW(k)$ at its discriminant element, with parameter $0$ and $q=p$ — consisting of a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $t.X$ over $E$, a natural number $t.n$ and a series $t.\rho$ over $E/pE$, with the following two properties. First, $t$ is admissible for $\iota$ and the structure map $W(k)\to W(k)/pW(k)\to E$: $t.X$ is special, of height $4$, and $t.\rho$ is an isogeny of height $4\,t.n$ from the base change of $\Phi$ to the reduction of $t.X$. Second, for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ that is a $\mathbb{Z}_p$-algebra and every ring homomorphism $y\colon E\to\Omega$ there are a Drinfeld datum $Q$ and a Deligne datum $d$ over $\Omega$ for $K=\mathbb{Q}_p$ and $\pi=p\in\mathbb{Z}_p$ such that: the base change $t.\mathrm{map}\,y$ is a Cartier quadruple for $Q$ with respect to $\iota$, $hc_\Phi$, $r_\Phi$ and the composed structure map (this comprises the $\mathcal O_D$-homomorphism property of $\rho$, isomorphisms of $Q.T_0,Q.T_1$ with the weight spaces of $\mathrm{Lie}$ intertwining $Q.\Pi_0,Q.\Pi_1$ with `lieVarpi`, and a description of the lattices $N_0,N_1$ and the maps $u_0,u_1$ at each prime through $\eta$-sections of the localised graded Cartier module data); $Q$ is the Drinfeld quadruple of $d$, meaning edge-nondegeneracy and that the kernels of $u_0,u_1$ are the lines of the base change of $d$ at the corresponding lattices; and the two explicit period conditions hold, namely $d.\mathrm{line}$ at the standard full lattice is the $\Omega$-span of $y(\xi)\otimes e_0+1\otimes e_1$, and $d.\mathrm{line}$ at the $g$-translate of the standard lattice is the image under `actBaseChange` of the $\Omega$-span of $1\otimes e_0+y(\eta)\otimes e_1$, where $\xi,\eta$ are the distinguished elements `edgeRingCharP.ξ`, `edgeRingCharP.η` of $E$ and $e_0,e_1$ the standard basis vectors.
--
--   This is the existence half of Drinfeld's local uniformisation statement in the form needed here: an explicit admissible family of special formal $\mathcal O_D$-modules over the whole reduced standard edge chart whose Cartier quadruple at each geometric point is the Drinfeld quadruple of a Deligne datum with tautological period lines. It is used by [`CerednikDrinfeld.SpecialFormal.Rigidified.exists_isAdmissible_isCartierQuadruple_isQuadrupleOf_of_line_eq_of_charP`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.SpecialFormal.Rigidified.exists_isAdmissible_isCartierQuadruple_isQuadrupleOf_of_line_eq_of_charP).
